  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 339112) has seen reduced federal contracting activity in FY2026 to date. The federal government obligated $814M in NAICS 339112 contracts so far, spread across 8,700 awards with an average award size of $93.5K. Obligations are down 49.5% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a peak in FY21 at $2.3B, then a general decline with FY22 at $1.1B, FY23 at $1.5B, FY24 at $2B, FY25 at $1.6B, and FY26 at $814M to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer with $691M in obligations in FY2026 to date. SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC, FIRST NATION GROUP LLC, and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC are the top three vendors in FY2026 to date by obligations. These figures are partial for the current fiscal year and reflect obligations rather than awarded contract ceilings or estimated future spending.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal demand for NAICS 339112 changed year over year?",
        "body": "Federal obligations fell 49.5% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $2.3B in FY21, $1.1B in FY22, $1.5B in FY23, $2B in FY24, $1.6B in FY25, and $814M in FY26 to date. The FY2026 to date total is a partial-year figure and represents obligations so far this fiscal year. The average award size in FY2026 to date is $93.5K across 8,700 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers and suppliers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer with $691M in obligations. The Department of Defense obligated $57M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $47.5M in FY2026 to date. SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC leads vendors with $131M, followed by FIRST NATION GROUP LLC with $97.5M and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC with $78.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
